# Paste this block into apps/facilitator/deploy/Caddyfile on the VPS (the single Caddy that
# fronts every public hostname on the box over the shared `edge` network), then reload Caddy.
# This file is a snippet on purpose: the checked-in facilitator Caddyfile is not modified here.
#
# The Cloudflare DNS record for agente.agentposhq.com must be DNS-only (grey cloud), not
# proxied: Caddy answers the ACME challenge itself to get the certificate.
#
# PRIVATE SURFACE. This host exposes the owner's mandate, purchase proposals and activity
# history. buyer-web now has its own login (owner account, scrypt, server-side sessions, CSRF
# and a password asked again before an approval), so this vhost is a plain reverse proxy: the
# temporary `basic_auth` block that used to stand in for the login, with its
# BUYER_WEB_BASIC_HASH and its /whatsapp/* exemption, must be REMOVED from the checked-in
# facilitator Caddyfile when this version is deployed. Keeping it only means typing two
# passwords, and it would break /login for a password manager.
#
# Still: never link this host publicly, never put it in a sitemap, a README example or the
# landing page. The only things that should ever call it are the owner's browser, the webhook
# POSTs from Meta/Twilio (they sign every request) and the owner's own `agentpos-buyer watch`
# daemon (bearer token).
agente.agentposhq.com {
	reverse_proxy buyer-web:8788
	encode gzip
}
